# A syntactically broken subquery must not emit lint warnings (DS2102, DS2103) on top of the syntax error.
mode: check
schema: orders(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real)
---- query
from (from orders | where 1 == 1 | sort by amount
---- expected
error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:6
  |
1 | from (from orders | where 1 == 1 | sort by amount
  |      ^                                           - the input ends before a `)`
  |      |
  |      this `(` is never closed
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
